+++ +#!/usr/bin/env bash
+++-+# Telegram notifier for the RL run. Runs on h200a, NOT on n82.
+++-+#
+++-+# n82 cannot reach api.telegram.org at all (http=000) -- Telegram is blocked
+++-+# from the China nodes. h200a reaches it fine, so the notifier lives there and
+++-+# pulls the run state over ssh via the existing china-trainer alias.
+++++# Drive the REAL watchdog scripts against a fake environment and assert on what
+++++# they actually do. Nothing real is touched: curl, ss, kill, sudo, docker,
+++++# nvidia-smi and sleep are all shadowed on PATH.
+++ +#
+++-+#   per step   -> message with step time, reward, running mean, and health
+++-+#   frozen run -> repeated CALL via CallMeBot (Telegram cannot place calls
+++-+#                 itself; CallMeBot rings your Telegram account)
+++-+#
+++-+# Credentials come from the environment so nothing secret lands in git:
+++-+#   TG_BOT_TOKEN   from @BotFather
+++-+#   TG_CHAT_ID     from @userinfobot ("Id")
+++-+#   CALLMEBOT_KEY  optional; from @CallMeBot_txtbot, enables the phone call
+++-+#
+++-+# Freeze definition: the TRAINER step counter has not advanced and the
+++-+# ORCHESTRATOR batch counter has not advanced for FREEZE_MIN minutes. Both must
+++-+# be stuck -- a slow batch alone is normal and must not page anyone.
+++++# The previous version of this file re-implemented each watchdog's decision as
+++++# a local shell function and tested THAT. It passed 18 of 18 while asserting
+++++# the opposite of the shipped behaviour: three cases still expected the tunnel
+++++# watchdog to refuse to rebuild on mass failure, a rule that was removed after
+++++# it froze the run for five hours. A test that mirrors the logic cannot catch a
+++++# change to the logic. Every case below runs the real script.
+++ +set -uo pipefail
+++ +
+++-+RUN=${RUN:-x22}
+++-+RUN_NAME=${RUN_NAME:-run_$RUN}
+++-+INTERVAL=${INTERVAL:-60}
+++-+FREEZE_MIN=${FREEZE_MIN:-15}
+++-+TG_BOT_TOKEN=${TG_BOT_TOKEN:-}
+++-+TG_CHAT_ID=${TG_CHAT_ID:-}
+++-+CALLMEBOT_KEY=${CALLMEBOT_KEY:-}
