++++++From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
++++++Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 21:12:47 +0000
++++++Subject: [PATCH 03/17] Derive pipeline stage buffer dtype from
++++++ optimization_dtype, not params
++++++
++++++The inter-stage buffers carry activations, but their dtype was taken from
++++++the first parameter of the stage module. Under bf16 weights those coincide,
++++++so it worked. Under quantization.dequantize_checkpoint = false the first
++++++parameter is float8_e4m3fn, so every hidden-state buffer was declared fp8:
++++++
++++++  PipeliningShapeError: Stage 1 forward outputs: value 0 has a dtype
++++++  mismatch: expected torch.float8_e4m3fn actual torch.bfloat16
++++++
++++++Scanning for the first real-float parameter is not a fix either -- an fp32
++++++weight_scale_inv can precede the bf16 weights and would declare the buffers
++++++fp32. optimization_dtype is the authoritative source for activations.
