++++++From 79815a37a68cff7aa5dac7d27f66c99d6f7933fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++++++From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
++++++Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 23:16:12 +0000
++++++Subject: [PATCH 06/17] Disable ac_offloading: it defaults ON and pins host
++++++ memory
++++++
++++++ActivationOffloadingConfig is the DEFAULT for ac_offloading
++++++(configs/trainer.py:173), not None, and no china config ever disabled it. It
++++++stashes activations in pinned host memory, so host usage tracks in-flight
++++++micro-batches rather than device memory.
++++++
++++++Measured on x18: 60 GB of /dev/zero per rank against 17 GB on the GPU, a
++++++3.5:1 ratio. 8 ranks x 60 GB = 480 GB on a 503 GB node. That is why neither
++++++FP8 (which halved device memory) nor expandable_segments (which cut reserved
++++++memory a third) moved the host ceiling at all.
++++++
++++++The [model.ac] comment already described this exact failure on this exact
++++++node; the setting was simply never turned off.
++++++
