+From 312a7d78d7bfdabf8f0f6f838970e7c2d894fcce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: DeltaVector1 <DeltaVector1@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 08:35:37 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 25/25] Lower max_inflight_rollouts to 128; add
+ apply_at_step.sh
+
+The engines were starving while the orchestrator believed it was saturating
+them. Sampled over 3 minutes at 246 in flight: Running oscillated 0 to 27 with
+Waiting at 0 on every sample and throughput between 0 and 890 tok/s. About 220
+requests were sitting in the SSH tunnels rather than at the engines.
+
+batch_size stays 1024, so the experiment is unchanged. Only the tunnel load
+drops: about 5 concurrent per tunnel instead of about 10.
+
+This also corrects a claim in the docs. "256 in flight holds, 1024 collapses"
+was wrong: every healthy reading behind it was sampled at a batch tail with
+single-digit in-flight. 256 oversubscribes as well.
+
+apply_at_step.sh waits for a given trainer step to finish and then restarts the
+orchestrator, which is the only way it re-reads its config. Restarting just
+after a step costs almost nothing because the next batch has barely started.
+It refuses to arm unless the staged value is really in the config, it leaves
+the trainer alone so the policy version stays valid, it defers to
+run_supervisor.sh rather than racing it, and it reports the one failure it
+cannot repair (a dispatcher pause, which needs a new run name).
+
